{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"immutab|configured CI|rule 2|acceptance test|test-author|builder commit|CI command|next-stage\\\" . --glob '\"'!conformance/factory/runs/*.out'\"' --glob '\"'!node_modules/**'\"' | sed -n '1,300p' && git branch --contains 66cde3e 2>/dev/null || true && git branch --contains aefdef1 2>/dev/null || true && git diff --stat 66cde3e 58823c9 && git diff --stat aefdef1 780e5bb && git diff 66cde3e 58823c9 -- conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js && git diff aefdef1 780e5bb -- conformance/app/server.js\"","aggregated_output":"./README.md:13:| `roles/` | Versioned prompt files for the five roles (planner, test-author, builder, reviewer, narrator) |\n./README.md:16:| `ci/` | Test-immutability check, branch protection, walking-skeleton pattern, rollback drill, Railway recipe |\n./README.md:24:2. The builder cannot edit tests — CI fails the PR if builder commits touch test files.\n./scripts/adapters/codex.sh:2:# Adapter: Codex CLI (model family B — test-author, reviewer).\n./conformance/factory/ledger.csv:2:2026-07-12,08:03:32,T-101,test-author,codex,1,1,0.3501,0\n./conformance/factory/ledger.csv:6:2026-07-12,08:22:15,T-101,test-author,codex,1,1,0.2515,0\n./conformance/factory/ledger.csv:10:2026-07-12,21:06:49,T-102,test-author,codex,1,1,0.2296,0\n./conformance/factory/ledger.csv:13:2026-07-12,21:17:55,T-102,test-author,codex,1,1,0.1672,0\n./FACTORY.md:8:- Copy from the kit: `envelope/ENVELOPE.template.md` → `factory/ENVELOPE.md`, `roles/` → `factory/roles/`, all three `workflows/` files (`ticket-flow.md`, `linear.md`, `evidence-rubric.md`) → `factory/`, `ci/test-immutability-check.sh` → `.github/scripts/`, `ci/github-actions-ci.template.yml` → `.github/workflows/ci.yml`.\n./FACTORY.md:21:- Three separate API keys minimum: factory-builder (family A), factory-reviewer/test-author (family B), product runtime. Named so console dashboards split spend cleanly.\n./FACTORY.md:30:- GitHub: branch protection per `ci/branch-protection.md`, the test-immutability check wired as a required status.\n./FACTORY.md:52:- [ ] Branch protection on; test-immutability check is a required status\n./conformance/factory/ENVELOPE.env:4:# - test-author (codex): $0.35\n./ci/test-immutability-check.sh:2:# test-immutability-check.sh — CI gate enforcing two mechanical rules that\n./ci/test-immutability-check.sh:61:      echo \"FAIL (rule 2, order): test commit $COMMIT ('$MSG') comes after implementation started — tests are frozen once building begins:\" >&2\n./ci/test-immutability-check.sh:71:  echo \"test immutability holds: test commits are pure and all precede implementation ($TEST_PATHS)\"\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:53:If this contract proves wrong during build or test-authoring, the ticket goes back to Ready for re-planning as a new version — do not silently change the shape.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:66:- 2026-07-12 21:06:49: test-author run completed through the wrapper; 3 contract tests committed in `18a7731`, all failing for the expected missing `approvals` field (0 passed, 3 failed); cost $0.2296.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:67:- 2026-07-12: builder implemented the frozen contract exactly (added `approvals` counts to the `/health` handler in `conformance/app/server.js`). `tests/health-approvals.test.js` (3/3) passes with exact `JSON.stringify` matches, confirming the implementation matches the frozen contract. **Blocked before commit:** this breaks all 4 pre-existing T-101 tests in `tests/health.test.js` (tests 1, 1b, 2, 3), which assert the `/health` body with `assert.deepStrictEqual(...)` against object literals that have no `approvals` key — `deepStrictEqual` rejects any extra key, so adding `approvals` anywhere in the response necessarily fails them. This is not an implementation bug: no server-side change can satisfy both \"exact frozen `approvals` shape per AC1–3\" and \"T-101's `health.test.js` stays green,\" because the latter was written before this contract existed and asserts an exact object with no extra keys. Per the builder's no-test-editing rule, I have not touched `tests/health.test.js` or any other test file, and have not committed the (correct, but suite-red) implementation change. Flagging for re-planning/reviewer adjudication: either (a) the contract stands and `health.test.js`'s 4 assertions need updating by the test-author/reviewer to tolerate/expect the new `approvals` key, or (b) the contract needs to change. Full suite as of this run: 11 passed, 4 failed (all 4 failures are the `health.test.js` ones described above; `health-approvals.test.js` and `conformance.test.js` are fully green).\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:68:- 2026-07-12 21:10:01: builder run completed through the wrapper and committed implementation plus its ticket note in `5e201e0`; new contract tests pass 3/3 but the full suite is red (11 passed, 4 pre-existing T-101 health tests failed); State → Blocked-Escalated; cost $0.6861495. Javier must decide whether the frozen additive contract stands and authorize test-author updates to `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js`, or send T-102 back to planner for a revised contract.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:69:- 2026-07-12: operator decision — the frozen additive T-102 contract stands; test-author is authorized to update only the exact-match `/health` expectations in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js` to include the frozen `approvals` object; State → In progress.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:70:- 2026-07-12: dispatch stopped because mandatory `next-stage.sh --ticket T-102` returned `RUN reviewer`, not `RUN test-author`; State → Blocked-Escalated. Javier must reconcile the sequencer/bookkeeping so it names the authorized test-author correction; no role run was launched.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:73:- 2026-07-12: dispatch refused before the authorized test-author fix because the mandatory sequencer reported `REFUSE reviewer ran 1 time(s) but only 0 verdict(s) are logged on /Users/sofiagonzalez/Projects/software-factory/conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md`; the verdict exists on the ticket branch in `a2aba87`, but the dispatcher cannot write it to main; State → Blocked-Escalated. Javier must reconcile the main ticket bookkeeping or sequencer source; no role run was launched.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:75:- 2026-07-12 21:17:55: test-author fix run completed through the wrapper; commit `81dd75e` changed only the four stale exact-match expectations in `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js`; full suite green (15 passed, 0 failed); cost $0.1672.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:76:- 2026-07-12 21:19:36: reviewer round 2: APPROVE — round 1 was addressed exactly, commit order and test-immutability discipline hold, implementation matches the frozen contract, and the full suite passes 15/15; cost $0.1258.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102.md:78:- 2026-07-12: Javier approved PR #2 and it was squash-merged to main as `1a62289`; the operator rebased the ticket branch before merge to satisfy the commit-order gate, and the test-immutability gate now exempts factory bookkeeping paths; State → Done.\n./ci/github-actions-ci.template.yml:25:  test-immutability:\n./ci/github-actions-ci.template.yml:31:      - name: builder commits must not touch tests\n./ci/github-actions-ci.template.yml:32:        run: .github/scripts/test-immutability-check.sh\n./ci/github-actions-ci.template.yml:38:# \"test-immutability\" (see ci/branch-protection.md).\n./ci/branch-protection.md:10:- Required status checks: `ci` and `test-immutability`, strict (branch up to date).\n./ci/branch-protection.md:27:    { \"type\": \"required_status_checks\", \"parameters\": { \"strict_required_status_checks_policy\": true, \"required_status_checks\": [ { \"context\": \"ci\" }, { \"context\": \"test-immutability\" } ] } },\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-101-bundle.md:49:All gates green: health tests 4/4, full conformance suite 8/8, immutability gate green. Reviewer verdict (round 2): APPROVE.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-101-bundle.md:59:| test-author | $0.60 (two rounds: $0.35 + $0.25) |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-101-bundle.md:65:Attempts: builder 2 (first hit its budget and was stopped), reviewer 2 rounds (round 1 requested stronger tests; test-author round 2 addressed it).\n./roles/planner.md:15:3. **Frozen contract**: the exact interface both the test-author and the builder code against — endpoint paths and shapes, UI selectors, fixture data, file locations. Once posted, the contract does not change; if it proves wrong, the ticket goes back to Ready and you re-plan it as a new version, noted on the ticket.\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:2:# next-stage.sh — mechanical stage sequencer. Given a ticket, computes the\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:8:#   FIX <builder|test-author> — reviewer requested changes; dispatcher picks\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:14:# Usage: next-stage.sh --ticket T-NNN   (FACTORY_ROOT anchors the factory dir)\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:29:[[ -n \"$TICKET\" ]] || { echo \"usage: next-stage.sh --ticket T-NNN\" >&2; exit 2; }\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:37:P=\"$(count_ok planner)\"; TA=\"$(count_ok test-author)\"; B=\"$(count_ok builder)\"\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:47:if [[ \"$TA\" -eq 0 ]]; then echo \"RUN test-author\"; exit 0; fi\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:68:# One rejection round: was a fix (test-author or builder success) completed\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:73:    else if (($4==\"builder\" || $4==\"test-author\") && last_r>0) fix=1\n./scripts/next-stage.sh:80:  echo \"FIX builder-or-test-author — reviewer round 1 requested changes; launch test-author if the tests were faulted, builder if the code was; then reviewer again\"\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:53:**After (test-author fix, commit `81dd75e`, re-verified live in this run):**\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:81:2. **Operator decision:** the frozen additive contract stands; test-author is authorized to update only the four stale exact-match expectations in `health.test.js` to include the `approvals` object.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:82:3. **Dispatcher-level sequencer mismatch:** the mandatory `next-stage.sh --ticket T-102` returned `RUN reviewer` instead of `RUN test-author`, blocking dispatch a second time. Operator resolution: no state surgery needed — the stale pre-T-102 assertions are the fault, not the sequencer, and `RUN reviewer` was the legally correct next step (reviewer adjudicates the conflict before any test edit).\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:86:7. **Reviewer round 2: APPROVE** — round 1 addressed exactly, commit order and test-immutability discipline hold, implementation matches the frozen contract, full suite passes.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:96:| `18a7731` | test: pin health approvals summary contract (test-author, new `health-approvals.test.js`, 3/3 failing as expected pre-implementation) |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:97:| `2ded4d0` | Log T-102 test-author completion |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:106:| `81dd75e` | Update stale health expectations for approvals summary (test-author fix, `conformance/app/tests/health.test.js`) |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:107:| `1221d86` | Log T-102 test-author fix completion |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:121:| test-author | 1 | codex | $0.2296 | New `health-approvals.test.js`, 3/3 failing as expected |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:124:| test-author | 2 | codex | $0.1672 | Applied the authorized fix; full suite green 15/15 |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-102-bundle.md:129:Attempts: planner 1, test-author 2 rounds, builder 1 (escalated rather than retried — the blocker was a genuine cross-ticket contract conflict, not a failed attempt), reviewer 2 rounds. Three additional dispatcher-level sequencer/bookkeeping escalations were resolved by the operator without spawning a new role run, so they carry no ledger cost.\n./scripts/run-agent.sh:63:  test-author|reviewer) DEFAULT_ADAPTER=\"codex\";;\n./conformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:15:| Test-immutability gate | passes on a clean builder branch; fails (exit 1) when a builder commit touches a test file |\n./conformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:25:5. **Ticket branches must merge, not delete.** During the immutability demo the ticket branch was deleted unmerged and the shakedown's own adapter fixes were nearly lost (recovered via reflog). The ticket-flow doc's rule — one branch, one PR, merged via approval — exists for a reason; the drill violated it and paid.\n./conformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:39:1. **Immutability gate bypass (both reviewers):** v1 exempted commits whose *message* contained `[test-author]` — a marker the builder itself controls. Rewritten to two identity-free mechanical rules: a commit may touch tests or code, never both (separation); and every test commit must precede every implementation commit (order). Verified: clean branch passes; late test edit fails rule 2; a mixed commit carrying the old marker fails rule 1.\n./conformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:42:4. **Cross-family rule became mechanical:** the wrapper now maps roles to adapters (builder/planner → claude-code; test-author/reviewer → codex) and refuses mismatches, instead of trusting prompts.\n./conformance/SHAKEDOWN-REPORT.md:48:The enforcement layer now holds against its own reviewers' attacks: no identity-based bypasses, anchored kill switch, reservation-based caps, mechanical cross-family and approval rules. Conformance suite: 8/8 green. Remaining honest gap, unchanged: **no ticket has yet run with real (non-mock) CLI agents** — that first real run is what the operator go-ahead buys, and it is the kit's final acceptance test.\n./ci/walking-skeleton.md:21:The operator clicking a working staging URL is the acceptance test. Until that click happens, no tickets are written, no backlog is cut, no other work proceeds.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-101.md:38:- 2026-07-12: test-author (codex) wrote 3 failing tests; verified they fail for the right reason (queue field missing). Committed a3e0b08. Finding: codex/claude sandboxes had to be bypassed for headless runs — containment moved to envelope + worktree + CI (adapters updated).\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-101.md:40:- 2026-07-12: reviewer (codex) round 1 REQUEST CHANGES — tests didn't assert HTTP 200 and a hard-coded pending:0 would pass. Test-author round 2 added both (a2f5a72, rebased before implementation; immutability gate green). Reviewer round 2: APPROVE.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:25:Before freezing the contract, enumerate every existing test that asserts exact response bodies this change would touch (`/health` queue counts, job objects in `/api/state`, the conformance suite's dead-letter test). If the contract necessarily breaks any of them, say so in the frozen contract and list the exact tests the test-author must amend *in the same test-authoring stage* — do not leave the collision for the builder to discover.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:52:- `attemptsSinceRetry` (number): attempts made since job creation, or since the most recent accepted retry, whichever is later. Incremented by `1` in the same worker tick that increments `attempts` (so it always equals `attempts` until the first retry, after which it runs ahead of `attempts` by the reset amount). This is the internal counter that drives the \"3 more attempts\" budget below — it is not itself a public promise beyond what AC1–AC4 require, but it is real state and will appear verbatim in `/api/state`, so the test-author may assert on it directly.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:63:If this contract proves wrong during build or test-authoring, the ticket goes back to Ready for re-planning as a new version — do not silently change the shape.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:74:**Conclusion: zero existing tests require amendment.** `tests/retry-dead.test.js` is a purely additive new file; the test-author does not need to touch any pre-existing test file for this ticket.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:87:- 2026-07-12: test author added `tests/retry-dead.test.js` with one acceptance test each for: retry-to-success and normal proposed action creation; exactly three fresh failed attempts with cumulative attempt history; immutable `409` refusal for both pending and done jobs; and persisted retry processing after `SIGKILL` + restart. The suite also covers the exact frozen unknown-job `404` response. All four criteria were expressible as tests; no demo-check-only items.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:88:- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) committed five frozen-contract checks at `b1d9ddf`; all five fail for the expected missing retry route/response behavior while all 20 existing tests pass; no product code or pre-existing tests changed; ledger cost $0.4673.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:90:- 2026-07-12 23:10:53: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — The accepted-retry transition is not inspected before the worker advances. An implementation that incorrectly clears `lastError` during the retry would pass all 25 tests. Add a controlled-worker assertion immediately after the `200` response verifying persisted state is `pending`, `attempts` and `lastError` are unchanged, `attemptsSinceRetry` is `0`, and `retries` is `1`. The frozen rule that `retries` increments by exactly one per accepted retry is only tested for the first retry. Add a second dead → retry cycle and assert the response and job record report `retries: 2` while preserving cumulative attempts and resetting only the fresh-attempt counter. Commit order and test immutability are correct. The pre-builder state reproduces 20 existing passes and 5 intended failures; the current full suite independently passes 25/25. The implementation otherwise matches the frozen contract and conventions. Cost $0.2527.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:92:- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) addressed reviewer round 1 at `66cde3e`; targeted suite passes 5/5 and full suite passes 25/25; only the acceptance tests and ticket log changed; ledger cost $0.3445.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:93:- 2026-07-12 23:16:39: reviewer round 2: REQUEST CHANGES — Commit `66cde3e` changes acceptance tests after implementation commit `aefdef1`, violating the test-immutability ordering convention. The configured CI command rejects it under rule 2. Reorder the corrected test commit before implementation, preserving content, then rerun CI. The two requested test gaps are correctly resolved, the implementation matches the frozen contract, and independent runs pass targeted 5/5 and full suite 25/25. Because this is round 2, State → Blocked-Escalated. The operator can either authorize history reordering or explicitly waive/change the immutability rule; the reviewer recommends reordering the commits because it preserves both the corrected tests and the existing convention. Cost $0.4161; completed role-run total $3.0093721, excluding the separate $1.50 reservation hold.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:94:- 2026-07-12 23:19:38: overlapping dispatcher execution launched a duplicate reviewer run after the round-2 run was already in flight. The duplicate reviewer reached the same REQUEST CHANGES verdict: tests pass targeted 5/5 and full 25/25, but the configured test-immutability gate fails because `66cde3e` follows `aefdef1`. No product files changed; ledger cost $0.4833. Ticket remains Blocked-Escalated pending the operator decision above.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:95:- 2026-07-12: operator adjudication accepted reviewer round 2's recommendation and reordered history with unchanged tree content: corrected acceptance tests now commit at `58823c9` before implementation at `780e5bb`; dispatcher independently verified the configured test-immutability gate passes and the full suite passes 25/25. The operator explicitly authorizes one additional reviewer round beyond the normal two-round limit, solely to verify reordered history and convert the verdict; rounds 1 and 2 content issues are resolved and adjudicated. State → In progress.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md:96:- 2026-07-12: State → Blocked-Escalated before reviewer round 3 because the mandatory worktree sequencer returned exactly: `ESCALATE reviewer requested changes twice — two-round limit reached, operator decides`. The sequencer has no operator-adjudication override input, so the dispatcher cannot mechanically launch the authorized reviewer through `run-agent.sh` without bypassing the binding stage gate. Javier must update/authorize an operator-controlled mechanism that makes `scripts/next-stage.sh --ticket T-104` return `RUN reviewer`; no reviewer round 3 or additional cost was incurred.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:38:- An approval object gains a `reason` key **only when/if it is rejected**, at the moment of rejection, and never removed or changed afterward (a second reject call is refused per above, so once set it is immutable).\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:49:If this contract proves wrong during build or test-authoring, the ticket goes back to Ready for re-planning as a new version — do not silently change the shape.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:59:**Conclusion: zero existing tests require amendment.** This is an audited result, not an assumption — the test-author does not need to touch any pre-existing test file for this ticket; `tests/reject-reason.test.js` is a purely additive new file.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:77:- 2026-07-12: test author added `tests/reject-reason.test.js` with one acceptance test each for: exact reason storage and response; null resolution for missing/non-string reasons; immutable rejection with exact `409`; and reason persistence across `SIGKILL` + restart. All four criteria were expressible as tests; no demo-check-only items.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:78:- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) committed four acceptance tests at `672a598`; new suite fails 4/4 for the expected missing behavior while all 15 existing tests pass; no implementation code changed; ledger cost $0.4749.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:79:- 2026-07-12: test-author verification expanded criterion 3 to cover every reachable non-pending status (`rejected`, `sent`, and `blocked_recipient`), asserting the exact `409` body and byte-for-byte unchanged approval record; the four acceptance tests still fail 4/4 for missing contract behavior, while all 15 existing tests pass. All criteria remain test-expressible; no demo-check items.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:80:- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) completed sequencer-selected verification at `f371048`; coverage now includes all reachable non-pending statuses, acceptance tests fail 4/4 as intended, and existing tests pass 15/15; ledger cost $0.4943.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:84:- 2026-07-12 22:36:03: reviewer round 1: REQUEST CHANGES — The frozen unknown-ID contract is untested. The builder changed reject-response serialization to remove the internal `code` field, but tests only verify exact `409` bodies. An implementation that fixes `409` while returning the wrong `404` body would pass all 19 tests. Add a test asserting an unknown approval returns HTTP `404` with exactly `{ \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such approval\" }`. Criteria 1–4 are otherwise adequately tested. Commit order and test immutability are correct, and the full suite independently passes 19/19. Cost $0.2206.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:85:- 2026-07-12: test-author (Codex) addressed reviewer round 1 by adding exact unknown-approval HTTP 404/body coverage at `257619e`; targeted suite passes 5/5 and full suite passes 20/20; only `tests/reject-reason.test.js` changed; ledger cost $0.2461.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:86:- 2026-07-12 22:40:20: reviewer round 2: APPROVE — The added test correctly asserts both HTTP `404` and the exact frozen body `{ \"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such approval\" }`; it would catch the prior leaked `code` field. Criteria 1–4 remain adequately tested. The implementation matches the frozen contract without scope creep, original acceptance tests were unchanged by the builder, the requested regression test is an additive later commit, commit order is correct, and the independently rerun full suite passes 20/20. Cost $0.1490.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103.md:87:- 2026-07-12: narrator (Claude Code) committed `conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md` at `60a3ef7` with fresh 20/20 tests and live local evidence; ledger cost $0.6907641999999999. State → Review, awaiting operator. Main-ledger total is $3.4570255; including the earlier real test-author run recorded only in the worktree ledger ($0.4749), full actual role-run cost is $3.9319255.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:100:- **Fix**: test-author added an exact `404` status + body test for an unknown approval id (commit `257619e`).\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:101:- **Round 2 — APPROVE**: new test correctly catches the prior leaked-`code`-field risk; all four criteria adequately tested; implementation matches the frozen contract with no scope creep; original acceptance tests untouched by the builder; commit order correct; full suite independently rerun 20/20.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:110:| `a29b4a0` | Log test-author run |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:111:| `672a598` | Add failing reject-reason acceptance tests (test-author, new `tests/reject-reason.test.js`, 4/4 failing as expected) |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:113:| `d58394d` | Log test-author verification |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:120:| `257619e` | Cover unknown approval rejection — add frozen 404 test (test-author fix) |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:126:**Internal change — low risk**, per the evidence rubric. No `external` label: rejecting a proposal cannot trigger a send — the outbox is untouched by this ticket, and this only adds metadata (`reason`) to an existing record. No schema migration is involved; the `reason` field is additive and only appears on already-rejected approvals. Worst plausible failure is a wrong or leaked `reason` value on a rejected approval, which the acceptance tests guard against with exact `deepStrictEqual` checks on the full approval object, including the non-pending/immutability and restart-persistence paths.\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:135:| test-author | 1 | codex | $0.4943 | New `tests/reject-reason.test.js`, expanded to cover all non-pending states, 4/4 failing as expected |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:138:| test-author | 2 | codex | $0.2461 | Added the requested regression test; full suite 20/20 |\n./conformance/factory/tickets/T-103-bundle.md:143:Attempts: planner 1, test-author 2 rounds, builder 1 (no retries), reviewer 2 rounds. Two additional dispatcher-level escalations (installed-vs-pinned Claude Code version warning; daily budget cap refusal at $8.97 spent) were resolved by the operator without spawning a new role run, so they carry no ledger cost of their own.\n./roles/dispatcher.md:20:Role runs launched in the sequence defined by `workflows/ticket-flow.md` (planner → test-author → builder → reviewer → narrator), ticket state moves with logged reasons, and escalations. Nothing else.\n./roles/dispatcher.md:25:- **The sequencer picks the stage, not you.** Before every launch, run `scripts/next-stage.sh --ticket <T-NNN>` and do what it says (`RUN <role>`, `FIX` — where you pick test-author vs builder from the reviewer's feedback — `AWAIT-OPERATOR`, `ESCALATE`, or `REFUSE`). If it refuses because a reviewer verdict is unrecorded, record the verdict line on the ticket first (`reviewer round N: APPROVE` / `reviewer round N: REQUEST CHANGES — reason`); never launch against its output.\n./roles/dispatcher.md:36:Ticket T-102 sits in Ready. Correct dispatch: launch planner via the wrapper; when it posts spec + branch, move to In progress with log line \"planner done, contract v1 posted\". Launch test-author; on its commit, launch builder in a fresh worktree; on green, launch reviewer. Reviewer replies REQUEST CHANGES — launch test-author round 2 with the reviewer's feedback in the task text, then reviewer round 2. On APPROVE, launch narrator; when the bundle is posted, move the ticket to Review with log line \"bundle posted, awaiting operator\" and stop. If instead the wrapper had refused the builder run with a ticket-budget message, the correct move is Blocked-Escalated with that exact message — not a retry, not an envelope edit.\n./roles/dispatcher.md:41:- v2: stage selection moved from judgment to mechanism — `scripts/next-stage.sh` is now mandatory before every launch; reviewer verdicts must be recorded on the ticket file (the sequencer blocks until they are).\n./roles/test-author.md:5:You write the failing acceptance tests for a spec'd ticket, before the builder starts. You run on a different model family than the builder, and you never write implementation code.\n./roles/README.md:8:- **Prompts are not enforcement.** Anything that must be true (budgets, test immutability, merge rights) is enforced by the wrapper, CI, or repo permissions. Prompts describe the job; mechanics enforce the rules.\n./roles/builder.md:5:You implement one spec'd ticket in a fresh git worktree until the test-author's tests pass. You cannot merge, you cannot edit tests, and you cannot change specs or contracts.\n./roles/builder.md:9:The ticket (spec, acceptance criteria, frozen contract) and the branch containing the test-author's failing tests.\n./workflows/linear.md:13:| In progress | Planner/test-author/builder working | agents |\n./workflows/linear.md:31:- [ ] Tests written (test-author: failing tests are first commits on branch)\n./workflows/ticket-flow.md:11:5. **CI** runs: lint, typecheck, tests, build, self-referential snapshots, test-immutability check.\n./workflows/ticket-flow.md:27:- Commit order is load-bearing: test commits (author: test-author) first, implementation commits (author: builder) after. The reviewer verifies authorship; CI verifies the builder's commits touch no test paths.\n conformance/app/server.js            | 23 +----------------------\n conformance/factory/tickets/T-104.md |  3 ---\n 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 25 deletions(-)\n conformance/app/tests/retry-dead.test.js | 124 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\n 1 file changed, 119 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
